IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `theft-nouns`
IMPORT `theft-s34-interpretation`

-- Theft Act 1968, sections 15 to 21: fraud, company officers, documents and
-- blackmail. Layer 1.
--
-- Sections 15, 15A, 15B and 16 (obtaining property, or a money transfer, or a
-- pecuniary advantage, by deception) keep their headings in this text but their
-- bodies show only dots. Nothing is encoded for them, and no rule here may be read
-- as saying that those offences do not exist elsewhere in the law.
--
-- "Dishonestly" in ss 17 and 20 is not the s 2 test: s 1(3) confines ss 2 to 6 to
-- s 1, and no exception in the Act reaches s 17 or s 20 (NOTES.md, fork 1). It is a
-- fact the person states.

§ `Sections 15 to 21 - false accounting, company officers, documents, blackmail`

§§ `Section 17 - false accounting`

-- src:121 | (1) Where a person dishonestly, with a view to gain for himself or another or with intent to cause loss to another,—
-- src:122 | (a) destroys, defaces, conceals or falsifies any account or any record or document made or required for any accounting purpose; or
-- src:123 | (b) in furnishing information for any purpose produces or makes use of any account, or any such record or document as aforesaid, which to his knowledge is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular;
-- src:124 | he shall, on conviction on indictment, be liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding seven years.
-- src:125 | (2) For purposes of this section a person who makes or concurs in making in an account or other document an entry which is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular, or who omits or concurs in omitting a material particular from an account or other document, is to be treated as falsifying the account or document.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 17 (src:121-125)
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`s 17(1) penalty for false accounting` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 7)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 17(2) (src:125)
GIVEN a IS A `False accounting facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) he is treated as falsifying the account or document` a MEANS
        a's `made or concurred in making an entry in it which is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
    OR  a's `omitted or concurred in omitting a material particular from it`

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 17(1)(a) (src:122)
GIVEN a IS A `False accounting facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1)(a) destroys, defaces, conceals or falsifies an account or accounting record or document` a MEANS
        a's `the thing is an account, or a record or document made or required for an accounting purpose`
    AND (    a's `destroyed it`
         OR  a's `defaced it`
         OR  a's `concealed it`
         OR  a's `falsified it`
         OR  `s 17(2) he is treated as falsifying the account or document` a)

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 17(1)(b) (src:123)
GIVEN a IS A `False accounting facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1)(b) in furnishing information produces or uses an account or record that he knows may be misleading` a MEANS
        a's `the thing is an account, or a record or document made or required for an accounting purpose`
    AND a's `in furnishing information for any purpose, produced or made use of it`
    AND a's `to his knowledge it is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 17(1) (src:121-124)
GIVEN a IS A `False accounting facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) guilty of false accounting` a MEANS
        a's `dishonest in falsifying or using the accounts`
    AND "with a view to gain for himself or another or with intent to cause loss to another" ...
            `s 34(2)(a) a view to gain or an intent to cause loss` (a's `the gain or loss in view in falsifying or using the accounts`)
    AND (    `s 17(1)(a) destroys, defaces, conceals or falsifies an account or accounting record or document` a
         OR  `s 17(1)(b) in furnishing information produces or uses an account or record that he knows may be misleading` a)

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 17(1) (src:124)
GIVEN a IS A `False accounting facts`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
`s 17(1) liable on conviction on indictment for false accounting` a MEANS
    IF `s 17(1) guilty of false accounting` a
    THEN `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `s 17(1) penalty for false accounting`
    ELSE `no offence under this section on these facts`

§§ `Section 18 - liability of company officers for certain offences by a company`

-- src:127 | (1) Where an offence committed by a body corporate under section ... 17 of this Act is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of any director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate, or any person who was purporting to act in any such capacity, he as well as the body corporate shall be guilty of that offence, and shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
-- src:128 | (2) Where the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its members, this section shall apply in relation to the acts and defaults of a member in connection with his functions of management as if he were a director of the body corporate.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 18 (src:127-128)
GIVEN o IS A `Company officer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18 guilty as an officer of the offence committed by the body corporate` o MEANS
        "an offence committed by a body corporate under section 17" ... `s 17(1) guilty of false accounting` (o's `the body corporate's offence`)
    AND "proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of" ... o's `it is proved that the offence was committed with his consent or connivance`
    AND "any director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate, or any person who was purporting to act in any such capacity, or (subsection (2)) a member managing its affairs" ...
            (    o's `he is a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate`
             OR  o's `he purported to act in such a capacity`
             OR  o's `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members and the act was his as a member in connection with his functions of management`)

-- s 18(1), "shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly": the
-- penalty is that of the offence the body corporate committed, s 17(1).
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 18(1) (src:127)
GIVEN o IS A `Company officer facts`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
`s 18 liable to be punished accordingly` o MEANS
    IF `s 18 guilty as an officer of the offence committed by the body corporate` o
    THEN `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `s 17(1) penalty for false accounting`
    ELSE `no offence under this section on these facts`

§§ `Section 19 - false statements by company directors, etc.`

-- src:130 | (1) Where an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association (or person purporting to act as such), with intent to deceive members or creditors of the body corporate or association about its affairs, publishes or concurs in publishing a written statement or account which to his knowledge is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular, he shall on conviction on indictment be liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding seven years.
-- src:131 | (2) For purposes of this section a person who has entered into a security for the benefit of a body corporate or association is to be treated as a creditor of it.
-- src:132 | (3) Where the affairs of a body corporate or association are managed by its members, this section shall apply to any statement which a member publishes or concurs in publishing in connection with his functions of management as if he were an officer of the body corporate or association.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 19 (src:130-132)
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`s 19(1) penalty for a false statement by an officer` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 7)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 19(1) (src:130)
GIVEN f IS A `False statement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19 guilty of a false statement by an officer` f MEANS
        (    f's `he is an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association, or purports to act as one`
         OR  f's `the affairs of the body corporate or association are managed by its members and he is a member publishing in connection with his functions of management`)
    AND f's `published or concurred in publishing a written statement or account`
    AND f's `to his knowledge the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
    AND (    f's `he intended to deceive members about its affairs`
         OR  f's `he intended to deceive creditors about its affairs`
         OR  f's `he intended to deceive a person who has entered into a security for the benefit of the body corporate or association`)

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 19(1) (src:130)
GIVEN f IS A `False statement facts`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
`s 19(1) liable on conviction on indictment for a false statement by an officer` f MEANS
    IF `s 19 guilty of a false statement by an officer` f
    THEN `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `s 19(1) penalty for a false statement by an officer`
    ELSE `no offence under this section on these facts`

§§ `Section 20 - suppression of documents`

-- src:134 | (1) A person who dishonestly, with a view to gain for himself or another or with intent to cause loss to another, destroys, defaces or conceals any valuable security, any will or other testamentary document or any original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, any court of justice or any government department shall on conviction on indictment be liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding seven years.
-- src:135 | (2) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:136 | (3) For the purposes of this section ... “valuable security” means any document creating, transferring, surrendering or releasing any right to, in or over property, or authorising the payment of money or delivery of any property, or evidencing the creation, transfer, surrender or release of any such right, or the payment of money or delivery of any property, or the satisfaction of any obligation.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 20 (src:134-136)
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`s 20(1) penalty for suppressing a document` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 7)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE

-- s 20(2) is shown as dots in this text and says nothing.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 20(3) (src:136)
GIVEN d IS A `Document facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(3) the document is a valuable security` d MEANS
        d's `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property`
    OR  d's `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property`
    OR  d's `it evidences the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right`
    OR  d's `it evidences the payment of money or the delivery of property`
    OR  d's `it evidences the satisfaction of an obligation`

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 20(1) (src:134)
GIVEN s IS A `Suppression facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) guilty of suppressing a document` s MEANS
        s's `dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing it`
    AND "with a view to gain for himself or another or with intent to cause loss to another" ...
            `s 34(2)(a) a view to gain or an intent to cause loss` (s's `the gain or loss in view in destroying, defacing or concealing it`)
    AND s's `destroyed, defaced or concealed it`
    AND (    `s 20(3) the document is a valuable security` (s's `the document`)
         OR  (s's `the document`)'s `it is a will or other testamentary document`
         OR  (s's `the document`)'s `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice`
         OR  (s's `the document`)'s `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a government department`)

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 20(1) (src:134)
GIVEN s IS A `Suppression facts`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
`s 20(1) liable on conviction on indictment for suppressing a document` s MEANS
    IF `s 20(1) guilty of suppressing a document` s
    THEN `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `s 20(1) penalty for suppressing a document`
    ELSE `no offence under this section on these facts`

§§ `Section 21 - blackmail`

-- src:138 | (1) A person is guilty of blackmail if, with a view to gain for himself or another or with intent to cause loss to another, he makes any unwarranted demand with menaces; and for this purpose a demand with menaces is unwarranted unless the person making it does so in the belief—
-- src:139 | (a) that he has reasonable grounds for making the demand; and
-- src:140 | (b) that the use of the menaces is a proper means of reinforcing the demand.
-- src:141 | (2) The nature of the act or omission demanded is immaterial, and it is also immaterial whether the menaces relate to action to be taken by the person making the demand.
-- src:142 | (3) A person guilty of blackmail shall on conviction on indictment be liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 21 (src:138-142)
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`s 21(3) penalty for blackmail` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 14)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE

-- s 21(1). A demand is unwarranted unless the person makes it in the belief both
-- that he has reasonable grounds for it and that the menaces are a proper means of
-- reinforcing it. Whether "menaces" are present is a fact the person states.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 21(1) (src:138-140)
GIVEN b IS A `Blackmail facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) the demand is unwarranted` b MEANS
    NOT (    b's `he believed he had reasonable grounds for making the demand`
         AND b's `he believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand`)

-- s 21(2): what is demanded, and whether the menaces relate to his own action,
-- are immaterial. The second is a field no rule reads; theft-cases-s15-21.l4
-- asserts that flipping it changes nothing.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 21(1) (src:138)
GIVEN b IS A `Blackmail facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) guilty of blackmail` b MEANS
        "with a view to gain for himself or another or with intent to cause loss to another" ...
            `s 34(2)(a) a view to gain or an intent to cause loss` (b's `the gain or loss in view in making the demand`)
    AND b's `made a demand with menaces`
    AND `s 21(1) the demand is unwarranted` b

@ref Theft Act 1968 s 21(3) (src:142)
GIVEN b IS A `Blackmail facts`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
`s 21(3) liable on conviction on indictment for blackmail` b MEANS
    IF `s 21(1) guilty of blackmail` b
    THEN `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `s 21(3) penalty for blackmail`
    ELSE `no offence under this section on these facts`
